From 1c374608abd47b59d47faae30a4e4bb447fffab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:06:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: use the display FE domain for J773g
 framebuffer

The firmware-owned display CPU power domain is disabled, so referencing it
can defer simpledrm until after appledrm removes conflicting framebuffers.
The late simpledrm device then survives alongside the native display and
appears as a second output to the compositor.

Use the managed display FE domain while retaining the DisplayPort PHY
dependency. This lets simpledrm register early enough for appledrm to remove
it during the normal framebuffer handoff.

Validation: the J773g DTB builds successfully. A fresh Fedora boot on the
M4 mini registers simpledrm at 0.1 seconds and hands over to appledrm at
4.2 seconds, with no late simpledrm output or runtime unbind required.

Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra)
Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
index e374ca61217cb..1ea7b1cec3e9c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
  * Keep the power-domains used for the HDMI port on.
  */
 &framebuffer0 {
-	power-domains = <&ps_dispext0_cpu>, <&ps_dptx_phy>;
+	power-domains = <&ps_dispext0_fe>, <&ps_dptx_phy>;
 };
 
 &sio_dart {
